# Regression fixture for inc-fiiq: killing one archon must not darken the other.
#
# Two torch archons stand one square apart, so each sits inside the other's
# magic circle.  The player kills the near one.  Map::RemoveField throws
# EV_FIELDOFF to everything the dead archon's field covered, including the
# survivor.  Before the fix that leave event removed every row with the same
# effect id -- the survivor's own included -- and Creature::StatiOff then
# reaped the survivor's field, so the survivor went dark while still alive.
#
# This is the scenario a player actually creates: kill one of a group.

@include chargen.keys

w
y
@choose "Genocide Everything"

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Celestials"
@choose "torch archon"
RIGHT ENTER

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Celestials"
@choose "torch archon"
RIGHT RIGHT ENTER

# Each RIGHT walks into the near archon and each y confirms the attack on a
# creature that is not hostile.  Fourteen swings kill it at this seed and stop
# short of reaching the far one.
RIGHT y RIGHT y RIGHT y RIGHT y RIGHT y RIGHT y RIGHT y RIGHT y RIGHT y RIGHT y
RIGHT y RIGHT y RIGHT y RIGHT y
ESC
@dump:after-kill
a
